# Developer Certificate of Origin — this project requires a sign-off.
#
# Every commit in a pull request must carry a `Signed-off-by:` trailer
# whose name and email match the commit author. CI checks this on every
# PR commit and the build fails without it.
#
# This template only REMINDS you. To actually add the trailer:
#
#     git commit -s              # adds it to this commit
#     git config format.signoff true   # adds it to every commit here
#
# Already committed without it? Re-sign the branch:
#
#     git rebase --signoff <base>
#
# Signing certifies that you wrote the patch, or otherwise have the
# right to submit it under the project's licence, and that you accept
# the DCO terms: https://developercertificate.org
#
# Anonymous or pseudonymous sign-offs are not accepted; the name and
# email must match your `git config user.name` / `user.email`.
#
# Note: git ignores this template when you pass `-m`. Use `git commit`
# with no `-m` to see it, or rely on `format.signoff` above.
#
# Lines beginning with `#` are stripped from the final message.
